    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear priority on stolen base upside, headlined by the stellar projection of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (77.20). He stands as our strongest play, bolstered by a prime leadoff spot and a favorable matchup against Taj Bradley; his ability to exploit the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery makes him a high-efficiency target for our scarcity-driven strategy. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** (68.98) anchors our outfield despite a slight platoon disadvantage, as his elite 0.475 xwOBA remains the most potent offensive weapon in our lineup. Meanwhile, **Colt Keith** (68.51) and **Trea Turner** (67.03) provide significant stability, with the latter benefiting from a +10% order bonus that elevates his ceiling against Manaea.\n\nOur bench composition was determined by strict adherence to the 40-point efficiency floor, leading to the exclusion of **Carson Benge** (38.04). While **Carson Benge** showed promise, his matchup against the southpaw Luzardo, combined with a dip in SP skill context, forced him below our threshold. **Casey Schmitt** (48.22) also narrowly missed the cut; while his platoon advantage against Bryan Woo was notable, his park factor penalized him enough to keep him on the pine. We are monitoring the 39% rain risk for **Caleb Durbin** and **Junior Caminero**, as both are positioned to capitalize on favorable wind conditions, provided the weather holds in their respective venues. Managers should keep a close watch on **Dillon Dingler**, whose status remains \"Lineup Pending,\" as any shift from the #3 spot could necessitate a tactical adjustment.",
